  "reasoning": "Statewide, New Jersey\u2019s Cook Partisan Voting Index is D+4, indicating the state has voted about 4 points more Democratic than the nation in recent presidential elections.[1][5] The most recent federal baseline is the 2024 presidential race, where Kamala Harris carried New Jersey by roughly 11 points statewide, with Essex County alone providing a margin of more than 140,000 votes that accounted for 55% of her statewide victory margin.[9][17] There is no evidence in the last 45 days of competitive statewide federal races or contrary polling; current-cycle coverage instead focuses on a single toss-up House district (NJ\u201107) against a backdrop of multiple strongly Democratic districts and entrenched Republican pockets, which supports viewing the overall federal lean of the state as Democratic.[3][7][8][10][13]",
